      "labels": {
        "en": {
          "title": "Alden",
          "summary": "Calist's father and the blacksmith of their village."
        },
        "de": {
          "title": "Alden",
          "summary": "Calists Vater und der Schmied ihres Dorfes."
        }
      },
      "fragments": [
        {
          "id": "alden-war-past",
          "visibility": {
            "mode": "reached-anchor",
            "story": "dragon-knight",
            "book": "volume-01",
            "anchor": "dk-v01-ch01-alden-war-gear",
            "chapter": "dk-v01-ch01"
          },
          "text": {
            "en": "Alden fought in the war and once served beside Corvin. He rarely tells Calist war stories, but he still carefully maintains the plain chainmail from that life.",
            "de": "Alden kämpfte im Krieg und diente einst an Corvins Seite. Er erzählt Calist kaum Kriegsgeschichten, hält aber das schlichte Kettenhemd aus dieser Zeit sorgfältig instand."
          },
          "readerLinks": [
            {
              "id": "alden-war-past-reader",
              "story": "dragon-knight",
              "book": "volume-01",
              "anchor": "dk-v01-ch01-alden-war-gear",
              "labels": {
                "en": "Open the related passage",
                "de": "Zugehörige Stelle öffnen"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "alden-teaches-craft",
          "visibility": {
            "mode": "reached-anchor",
            "story": "dragon-knight",
            "book": "volume-01",
            "anchor": "dk-v01-ch04-first-independent-work",
            "chapter": "dk-v01-ch04"
          },
          "text": {
            "en": "Alden teaches practically: work must hold, mistakes are done again, and usefulness matters more than making something impressive.",
            "de": "Alden unterrichtet praktisch: Arbeit muss halten, Fehler werden noch einmal gemacht, und Brauchbarkeit zählt mehr als Eindruck."
          },
          "readerLinks": [
            {
              "id": "alden-teaches-craft-reader",
              "story": "dragon-knight",
              "book": "volume-01",
              "anchor": "dk-v01-ch04-first-independent-work",
              "labels": {
                "en": "Open the related passage",
                "de": "Zugehörige Stelle öffnen"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "alden-winter-illness",
          "visibility": {
            "mode": "reached-anchor",
            "story": "dragon-knight",
            "book": "volume-01",
            "anchor": "dk-v01-ch07-alden-illness",
            "chapter": "dk-v01-ch07"
          },
          "text": {
            "en": "A winter illness keeps Alden away from the forge longer than he wants, leaving Calist to keep the village's repair work moving.",
            "de": "Eine Winterkrankheit hält Alden länger von der Schmiede fern, als er akzeptieren will. Calist übernimmt in dieser Zeit die Reparaturen des Dorfes."
          },
          "readerLinks": [
            {
              "id": "alden-winter-illness-reader",
              "story": "dragon-knight",
              "book": "volume-01",
              "anchor": "dk-v01-ch07-alden-illness",
              "labels": {
                "en": "Open the related passage",
                "de": "Zugehörige Stelle öffnen"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "alden-war-gear-gift",
          "visibility": {
            "mode": "reached-anchor",
            "story": "dragon-knight",
            "book": "volume-01",
            "anchor": "dk-v01-ch09-chainmail-sword",
            "chapter": "dk-v01-ch09"
          },
          "text": {
            "en": "Before Calist joins the soldiers, Alden brings out the chainmail and sword he carried in the war and gives them to his son.",
            "de": "Bevor Calist sich den Soldaten anschließt, holt Alden Kettenhemd und Schwert hervor, die er im Krieg getragen hat, und gibt sie seinem Sohn."
          },
          "readerLinks": [
            {
